Rachel Andrew is a British web developer, writer and speaker. She began building websites in 1996, and after the dot-com crash she started her own business.

## Building the web

In 2001 she founded edgeofmyseat.com, a web development company. It went on to make Perch, a small content management system, and Notist, a tool for speakers to share their talks. She was also a member of the Web Standards Project.

## Teaching CSS layout

When CSS Grid Layout was being developed, Andrew became one of its best-known teachers. She wrote articles and books, built a large set of examples at gridbyexample.com, and spoke about it at conferences around the world. She also became an invited expert in the W3C CSS Working Group, helping shape the specifications herself.

- **2004:** Published the first edition of *The CSS Anthology*.
- **2016:** Published *Get Ready for CSS Grid Layout*, and updated *HTML5 for Web Designers* with Jeremy Keith for its second edition.
- **2017:** Published *The New CSS Layout* and became editor-in-chief of *Smashing Magazine*.

She has written or co-written more than twenty books on web development. She later joined Google as a technical writer, working on web documentation including MDN Web Docs.

